    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Step 2a: Building the URL Safely"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The first thing our API function does is construct the request URL."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "const url = `https://api.programiz.pro/api/demo/javascript/jobs?title=${encodeURIComponent(keyword)}`;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We use a template literal to build the URL dynamically. The encodeURIComponent() function is critical here."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For instance, if someone searches for \"C++ developer\", the + and space characters need special encoding to work in a URL."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Without encoding:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "https://api.programiz.pro/api/demo/javascript/jobs?title=C++ developer"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "With encoding:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "https://api.programiz.pro/api/demo/javascript/jobs?title=C%2B%2B%20developer"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The second URL is valid. The first would break. encodeURIComponent() ensures we get the second URL."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
